    <strong>TL;DR — do not accept this branch as-is.</strong>
    The change adds substantial, well-tested machinery: fail-fast environment validation, adaptive bounded log scans, exact timestamp-to-block lookup, claim reconstruction over the protocol’s full claim window, and a gate that avoids staking deposits on unsettled reads. However, the Arb→Gnosis path passes Sepolia block numbers into Chiado contract reads. That breaks claiming and disputed-claim resolution on that route. A second introduced liveness bug makes a cold-started claimer stop when no recent <code>Claimed</code> log exists. Heartbeat calls are removed while heartbeat code and configuration remain. The supplied independent review therefore records <strong>NEEDS-CHANGES</strong> despite all 151 executed tests passing.
